(
    bones: {
        // The LEGS ARE DELIBERATELY ABSENT.
        //
        // They used to carry a baked knee flex, authored in the synthetic
        // rig's facing convention. A stored rotation cannot know which rig
        // it will drive, and `puppet_base.gltf` faces the opposite way — so
        // the baked bend rendered as a BACKWARD-bending knee on the real
        // character, and no runtime correction could reach it because the
        // value was already in the file.
        //
        // The knee flex is now applied at runtime by
        // `stance::stance_on_rig`, which derives the bend direction from
        // the rig's own measured geometry. Do not re-bake it here.
        //
        // What remains is the Mixamo-derived upper body, which is
        // rig-independent: arms, spine, neck and head.
        //
        // EXCEPT the neck's angle. The clip bows it 41.27 degrees, and on
        // the rendered rig that had the character staring 30.5 degrees at
        // the floor. 10.64 degrees about the same axis levels the gaze
        // exactly, over the clip's own spine curve — which is kept, because
        // it is what holds the body's centre of mass 4.8 cm ahead of the
        // ankles, as Winter's quiet stance does. Solved on
        // `gltf_rig::puppet_base_as_rendered`; pinned by
        // `poses::tests::the_relaxed_stand_stands_upright_and_balanced`.
        "Neck": (
            swing: (
                axis: (-0.9990133, 0.0, -0.0444121),
                degrees: 10.6437,
            ),
            twist_degrees: 0.0,
        ),
        "LeftShoulder": (
            swing: (
                axis: (0.0, -0.6989497, 0.71517086),
                degrees: 25.556078,
            ),
            twist_degrees: 0.0,
        ),
